var help_default = "Usage: akm-migrate <command> [options]\n\nThe one migration tool for an akm installation. The CLI proper reads every\nshape akm has ever written (in memory, with a warning); `apply` makes the\ncurrent shape durable on disk. `status` and `apply` run every step, in\norder, and print one combined JSON plan (exit 1 when any step is blocked):\n\n  1. config.json rewritten in its current shape (unknown keys dropped, the\n     `engines`/`defaults` form converted to `connections`/`harnesses` with\n     `defaults.improveStrategy` as `improve.strategy`, `configVersion` set\n     to the current value) -- backed up first. A config in the pre-0.9.15\n     source layout is refused, not converted: run this under akm 0.9.x. Keys akm no longer reads from config (an engine's\n     `apiKeyFile`, a literal or `${secrets/...}` `apiKey`, and the same on a\n     connection or `embedding`) move to\n     credentials.json, one note per key (never its value); a key that cannot\n     be moved stays on the connection as `apiKey`, with a note. The retired\n     models.json is folded into the models of the connections and harnesses\n     it names (the entries it cannot place are listed in the notes), then\n     moved to the config backups. A connection or harness akm cannot use stays in the\n     file as written, with a note on what to fix\n  2. pending state.db migrations, historical-destructive ones included,\n     with a verified sibling safety copy (the only path that admits them)\n  3. task files at version 2 or 3, and version 4 files still carrying the\n     retired `schedule[].enabled` key, rewritten as task source v4 under\n     one backup directory per run. A task file named on the command line\n     is converted to task source v5 (`version: 5-beta.<n>`) instead, after\n     the same check a start makes of it; no file is converted that is not\n     named. What a version 4 task did that version 5 does not (values given\n     to steps as AKM_PARAMS/AKM_STEPS, values appended to prompts) is\n     listed per file, to change by hand, and a file with no version 5 form\n     is left as it is and reported. A workflow file named on the command\n     line (`workflows/<name>.md`) is not changed: a new task file\n     `tasks/<name>.yml` is made from it, after the same check, when the\n     workflow compiler reads it and every step is a prose step or an\n     exec step of plain words. A workflow that cannot convert (a fan-out,\n     a child workflow, a `${...}` in a step that is not an input or an\n     earlier step, and the rest) is reported with `reason`, `detail` and\n     `guidance`: what to change in the workflow, then run again. An\n     existing task file is never overwritten. Workflows are removed in 0.11\n  4. the retired `engine:` key on commands, agents, workflows and task\n     sources rewritten to `connection:` or `harness:` by what the name is\n     now, under one backup directory per run\n  5. refs in the text files akm indexes in writable bundles that still use\n     the spelling from before refs became bundle paths (`knowledge/WORK/x`,\n     now `WORK/x`), in frontmatter and body: `[bundle//]<folder>/<path>`,\n     `<type>:<path>` and `wiki:<path>`, rewritten under one backup directory\n     per run. An old spelling that is now another file's ref is not\n     rewritten, only listed\n  6. bundle policy in writable bundles: an asset's `lint_skip:` frontmatter\n     is stripped (lint skips live in the bundle's `lint.skip` config); a\n     `.gitignore` with the old marker for tracking env and secrets adds\n     `\"tracked-secrets\": [\"**\"]` to that bundle's `lint.skip`. `.gitignore` is\n     never modified. The config is written first, the files under one backup\n     directory per run\n  7. proposals in state.db that an older akm recorded with the files they\n     change (`changes[].path`, a target directory) rewritten as the current\n     record, which names assets by ref, in one transaction after a copy of\n     state.db (`state.db.pre-proposal-records.bak`); until then every command\n     reads them as converted and says so once\n  8. index rows written before the index was keyed by ref (a keyring's or\n     vault's entries, which held a path inside the bundle's root) re-keyed\n     to hold no path, in one update that changes no column and not the\n     layout; until then every command reads them as they are meant\n  9. superseded residue removed: pre-0.9.0 `.akm` leftovers in the stash,\n     and the transaction-journal, maintenance-barrier, lock-mutex and\n     version-stamp files older releases kept under $DATA, $STATE and $CONFIG\n\n`akm migrate status|apply` wraps this executable; `akm upgrade` runs\n`apply` after its install step, so an image that ships akm can put either\nin its entrypoint (a current installation is a no-op).\n\nCommands:\n  status [<file>...]   Inspect every pending migration without changing anything,\n                       and report what apply would make of the named task and\n                       workflow files.\n  apply [--dry-run] [<file>...]\n                       Back up and apply every pending migration, and convert the\n                       named task files to task source v5 and the named workflow\n                       files to new v5 task files.\n";

